A||||6||Fearless Freep||GT Side Windows With Scoops||||1||
Z||000000||Fearless Freep||09-18-2000||07:13 PM||||Got a question.....exactly how functional are the scoops on the side windows?  I mean I know all the hub-bub about the vacuum effect behind the rear window etc.etc..etc...I guess my question is...Does this really help or hurt the cooling? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||09-18-2000||07:57 PM||||if only I had the cash... I'd love to get one of those digital electric berometers&lt;sp?&gt; and just start trying to figure it all out. Just think, you could litteraly pin point the exact optimum placement for a rear deck scoop (to the the most vaccumm) and you could figure out exactly what the effects of T-Tops, sun roofs, notch/fast backs, scoops and all that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-18-2000||09:37 PM||||It depends on just how the scoop is done on the GT sail. Small diferances in the scoope design could make big diferances in how they flow air and how they effect the venting of the engine.<P>Actually this could probly be figured out, at least crudly, with a spare MAP sensor, a DVM, and a 5v power supply. You might not have barrometer numbers but it would at least tell you if a change has helped or hurt. The MAP sensor is pretty sensitive and should have more than enough range.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||09-18-2000||10:32 PM||||I've driven a GT with these scoops. There is absolutely NO rear quarter visibility.. I had a heck of a time backing out of a parking space at a McDonalds... no matter what the performance gains (if any) from these scoops... I'd never get them.. but, that's just my opinion.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||13
Z||000004||Cooter||09-18-2000||10:58 PM||||I had those on my Se fastback conversion and I hated them! I wish that I had saved my lunch money and bought the Fiero Warehouse reproductions. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||09-19-2000||11:46 AM||||Whew! And I thought I was missing out.  I just ordered some factory ones a couple weeks ago.  I'm glad to hear there not all that there "cut out" to be. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||09-22-2000||06:58 PM||||They are sorta functional. They scoop air, but they don't really direct it anywhere. It helps blow the burning oil out of the decklid vents (Yeah, yeah, yeah, I have to fix that). The visiblility thing is the real killer though. If your going to get them, spend the extra money on the ones with the little windows on them.<BR> If the guy I bought the car from wouldn't have put them on, I'd have never done it.||||reg||1
